cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TiNews: A Diagnostic Benchmark for Tibetan News Understanding under Syllable Orthography Constraints"
message: "If you use TiNews, the ISR metric, or any result in this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "[AUTHOR NAME]"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/[ORCID]"
    email: "[EMAIL]"
abstract: >-
  TiNews is a diagnostic benchmark for Tibetan news understanding that exposes a
  class of systematic structural failures invisible to standard metrics such as
  perplexity or BLEU. It introduces the Illegal Syllable Rate (ISR), a syllable-level
  orthography diagnostic, and frames compression behaviour through an Information-
  Bottleneck / KL decomposition. The benchmark covers three tasks (7-class news
  classification, sentence-level continuation, and abstractive summarization with
  keywords) and ships with all experimental results, figure data, and significance
  tests reported in the accompanying paper.
keywords:
  - Tibetan
  - NLP benchmark
  - low-resource
  - orthography
  - information bottleneck
  - diagnostic evaluation
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/[GITHUB USERNAME]/TiNews"
